 and 25 hp has to be transmitted. The coefficient of friction μ between the belt and pulley material is 0.25. Determine whether the belt slip is possible for the following angles of contact: (a) 150° and 100°; (a) The belt will slip at both 150° and 100°. (b) The belt slip is independent of the angle of contact. (c) The belt will not slip at 150° but tends to slip at 100°. (d) The belt will not slip at either angle if the power transmitted is reduced to 20 hp. (e) The belt will slip at 100° only if the engine speed is increased to 1200 rpm. (f) The belt will slip at both angles if the coefficient of friction is reduced to 0.2. (g) The belt will not slip at both 150° and 100°. (h) The belt will not slip at 100° but tends to slip at 150°. (i) The belt will slip at 150° if the power transmitted exceeds 30 hp. (j) The belt will slip at 150° but not at 100°. Answer with the correct option letter and its content.", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The belt will not slip at 150° but tends to slip at 100°.", "expert_answer": "(c) The belt will not slip at 150° but tends to slip at 100°.", "expert_latency_s": 9.9, "stall_ms": 26, "relay_ms": 622}
