{"id": "q0363", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 2.67, "n_chunks": 3, "scores": [0.5176, 0.417, 0.3467], "eot_score": 0.3796, "eot_read_ms": 26, "reference_answer": "Cornwall", "query": "Yarg and gevrik are cheeses from which county?", "transcript": "Yarg and Gevrek are cheeses from which county?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Yarg and Gevrek are cheeses from the Antalya region of Turkey. Antalya is a county in southwestern Turkey known for its diverse and high-quality dairy products, including these traditional cheeses. Yarg is typically made from ewe's milk or mixed sheep and goat's milk, while Gevrek is often made exclusively from ewe's milk.", "answer_ms": 2026}
{"id": "q0374", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 4.74, "n_chunks": 5, "scores": [0.4225, 0.4909, 0.3119, 0.5791, 0.4471], "eot_score": 0.754, "eot_read_ms": 26, "reference_answer": "GREAT DANE", "query": "What breed of dog is Marmaduke in the newspaper cartoon strip of that name?", "transcript": "What breed of dog is Marmaduke in the newspaper cartoon strip of that name?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Marmaduke is a Great Dane.", "expert_answer": "Marmaduke is a **Great Dane**.", "expert_latency_s": 1.24, "stall_ms": 28, "relay_ms": 297}
{"id": "q0385", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 1.45, "n_chunks": 2, "scores": [0.5076, 0.3596], "eot_score": 0.7054, "eot_read_ms": 30, "reference_answer": "Toy", "query": "What is a Jacob's Ladder?", "transcript": "What is a Jacob's Ladder?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "A Jacob's ladder can refer to several things, depending on context. It might be the biblical stairway to heaven seen by Jacob in a dream from the Book of Genesis. Or it could be an electrical device where an arc climbs between two rods. There's also a classic toy made of wooden blocks and ribbons that creates a cascading effect when pulled apart. It can also refer to a type of rope ladder used historically or even a flowering plant called Polemonium.", "expert_answer": "A **Jacob’s ladder** can refer to several things, depending on context:\n\n1. **Biblical reference:** The ladder or stairway to heaven seen by Jacob in a dream in the Book of Genesis.\n2. **Electrical device:** A high-voltage apparatus where an electric arc climbs upward between two diverging metal rods.\n3. **Toy:** A folding wooden-block toy connected by ribbons that creates a cascading illusion.\n4. **Knot/rope ladder:** A type of rope ladder used on ships or for climbing.\n5. **Plant:** A flowering plant in the genus *Polemonium*, commonly called Jacob’s ladder.", "expert_latency_s": 4.08, "stall_ms": 39, "relay_ms": 2925}
{"id": "q0391", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 3.15, "n_chunks": 4, "scores": [0.4246, 0.4945, 0.4228, 0.4329], "eot_score": 0.6989, "eot_read_ms": 28, "reference_answer": "Percy LeBaron Spencer", "query": "Who invented the microwave oven in 1945?", "transcript": "Who invented the microwave oven in nineteen forty five?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Percy Spencer invented the microwave oven in 1945.", "expert_answer": "Percy Spencer invented the microwave oven in 1945.", "expert_latency_s": 2.56, "stall_ms": 37, "relay_ms": 476}
{"id": "q0405", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 2.04, "n_chunks": 3, "scores": [0.4733, 0.1732, 0.3996], "eot_score": 0.28, "eot_read_ms": 27, "reference_answer": null, "query": "How many months have 28 days?", "transcript": "How many months have twenty eight days?", "mode": "local", "answer": "All 12 months have **at least 28 days**. However, if the question is asking how many months have **exactly 28 days**, that's only true for **February** in **common years** — but even then, February has **28 days only in non-leap years** and 29 in leap years. So strictly speaking, no month has *always exactly 28 days*, except when it happens occasionally for February in common years. But again, all months have at least 28 days, so technically, **all 12 months** have 28 days or more.", "answer_ms": 4194}
{"id": "q0414", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 5.67, "n_chunks": 6, "scores": [0.4197, 0.2749, 0.2881, 0.3184, 0.2388, 0.2416], "eot_score": 0.4827, "eot_read_ms": 30, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Imagine you are the last person on Earth. Write a diary entry describing your thoughts and feelings.", "transcript": "Imagine you are the last person on Earth. Write a diary entry describing your thoughts and feelings.", "mode": "local", "answer": "**Diary Entry – Day 472**", "answer_ms": 351}
{"id": "q0424", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 2.42, "n_chunks": 3, "scores": [0.335, 0.3925, 0.3775], "eot_score": 0.4121, "eot_read_ms": 26, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Give me some examples of metamorphic rocks.", "transcript": "Give me some examples of metamorphic rocks.", "mode": "local", "answer": "Sure! Here are some common examples of metamorphic rocks, which form from the transformation of existing rocks under heat, pressure, or chemically active fluids during tectonic processes like mountain building or deep burial beneath Earth's surface. Examples include the following rock types and their typical parent rocks or origins. 1. Gneiss – often forms from granite or basalt when subjected to high heat and pressure over long periods; characterized by banded layers due to segregation of minerals into light and dark bands. 2. Schist – develops from shale, limestone, or basalt at moderate to high temperatures and pressures; notable for its schistosity, a tendency to split along flat planes due to aligned mica minerals like muscovite or biotite. 3. Slate – typically forms from shale under low-grade metamorphism; it splits easily into thin sheets because of the alignment of clay minerals such as illite or chlorite. 4. Marble – created when limestone or dolostone is metamorphosed in the presence of heat and often carbon dioxide-rich fluids; composed mainly of recrystallized calcite or dolomite with distinctive foliated or non-foliated textures. 5. Phyllite – an intermediate stage between slate and schist, formed from shale or mudstone; has a silky sheen due to fine-grained mica minerals and can be split along wavy planes. 6. Quartzite – forms from sandstone through high-pressure and moderate-temperature metamorphism; retains much of the original quartz grains but becomes very hard and non-foliated. These rocks are key components of Earth's crust and provide important clues about past geological conditions where they formed.", "answer_ms": 11085}
{"id": "q0435", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 1.98, "n_chunks": 2, "scores": [0.4219, 0.4252], "eot_score": 0.8179, "eot_read_ms": 35, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Who are the top NFL Quarterbacks?", "transcript": "Who are the top NFL quarterbacks?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "As of recent NFL seasons, the top quarterbacks are generally considered to include:\\n\\n1. **Patrick Mahomes — Kansas City Chiefs**\\n2. **Josh Allen — Buffalo Bills**\\n3. **Lamar Jackson — Baltimore Ravens**\\n4. **Joe Burrow — Cincinnati Bengals**\\n5. **Jalen Hurts — Philadelphia Eagles**\\n6. **Justin Herbert — Los Angeles Chargers**\\n7. **C.J. Stroud — Houston Texans**\\n8. **Dak Prescott — Dallas Cowboys**\\n9. **Matthew Stafford — Los Angeles Rams**\\n10. **Aaron Rodgers — New York Jets**\\n\\nIf ranking by career legacy, **Mahomes, Rodgers, Stafford, and Russell Wilson** would be higher. If ranking by current form and upside, **Mahomes, Allen, Jackson, Burrow, Stroud, and Herbert** are usually near the top.", "expert_answer": "As of recent NFL seasons, the top quarterbacks are generally considered to include:\n\n1. **Patrick Mahomes — Kansas City Chiefs**\n2. **Josh Allen — Buffalo Bills**\n3. **Lamar Jackson — Baltimore Ravens**\n4. **Joe Burrow — Cincinnati Bengals**\n5. **Jalen Hurts — Philadelphia Eagles**\n6. **Justin Herbert — Los Angeles Chargers**\n7. **C.J. Stroud — Houston Texans**\n8. **Dak Prescott — Dallas Cowboys**\n9. **Matthew Stafford — Los Angeles Rams**\n10. **Aaron Rodgers — New York Jets**\n\nIf ranking by career legacy, **Mahomes, Rodgers, Stafford, and Russell Wilson** would be higher. If ranking by current form and upside, **Mahomes, Allen, Jackson, Burrow, Stroud, and Herbert** are usually near the top.", "expert_latency_s": 5.96, "stall_ms": 34, "relay_ms": 6737}
{"id": "q0447", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 1.94, "n_chunks": 2, "scores": [0.4446, 0.3075], "eot_score": 0.6384, "eot_read_ms": 32, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Can I run MacOS on a Windows PC?", "transcript": "Can I run Mac OS on a Windows PC?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Generally, **no—not officially**. macOS is licensed by Apple to run only on Apple-branded hardware, so installing it directly on a typical Windows PC isn’t supported and may violate Apple’s terms. While some technically savvy users have managed to get it working in what’s called a “Hackintosh,” it can be unstable and difficult to maintain. Running macOS in a virtual machine on a Windows PC is also usually not permitted under Apple’s licensing rules. If you need macOS functionality, your best bets are using a Mac, cloud-based Mac services, or alternative tools like WSL/Linux that offer similar capabilities.", "expert_answer": "Generally, **no—not officially**.\n\n- **macOS is licensed by Apple to run only on Apple-branded hardware** (Macs). Installing it directly on a typical Windows PC (“Hackintosh”) is **not supported** and usually violates Apple’s license terms.\n- It may be **technically possible** on some PC hardware, but it can be difficult, unstable, and updates/drivers may break.\n- Running macOS in a VM on a Windows PC is also generally **not permitted by Apple’s licensing**.\n\nIf you need macOS, the supported options are:\n1. Use a **Mac**.\n2. Use a **cloud Mac service** for development/testing.\n3. If you only need macOS-like tools, use **WSL/Linux**, cross-platform apps, or remote access to a Mac.", "expert_latency_s": 4.68, "stall_ms": 39, "relay_ms": 3976}
{"id": "q0459", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 3.27, "n_chunks": 4, "scores": [0.3179, 0.3567, 0.4851, 0.4663], "eot_score": 0.5734, "eot_read_ms": 28, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What are some basic spirits you should have at your bar", "transcript": "What are some basic spirits you should have at your bar?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Some basic spirits to keep at a bar are vodka, gin, rum, tequila, whiskey, brandy or cognac, and vermouth. With these in your arsenal, you can make most classic cocktails and satisfy the majority of common drink requests.", "expert_answer": "Some basic spirits to keep at a bar are:\n\n- **Vodka**\n- **Gin**\n- **Rum** — light and/or dark\n- **Tequila**\n- **Whiskey** — bourbon, rye, or Scotch\n- **Brandy or Cognac**\n- **Vermouth** — sweet and dry, for cocktails like Martinis and Manhattans\n\nWith these, you can make many classic cocktails and serve most common drink requests.", "expert_latency_s": 2.88, "stall_ms": 37, "relay_ms": 1730}
{"id": "q0463", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 2.49, "n_chunks": 3, "scores": [0.4426, 0.355, 0.3924], "eot_score": 0.5717, "eot_read_ms": 31, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Does Las Vegas have a professional hockey team?", "transcript": "Does Las Vegas have a professional hockey team?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Yes. Las Vegas has an NHL team called the Vegas Golden Knights.", "expert_answer": "Yes. Las Vegas has an NHL team: the **Vegas Golden Knights**.", "expert_latency_s": 1.37, "stall_ms": 39, "relay_ms": 433}
{"id": "q0471", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 3.49, "n_chunks": 4, "scores": [0.3671, 0.3373, 0.5313, 0.5271], "eot_score": 0.6946, "eot_read_ms": 27, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Write a brief summary of Nezami Ganjavi's Layli and Majnun.", "transcript": "Nizami Ganjavi's Layli and Majnun.", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Sure! Nizami Ganjavi’s *Layli and Majnun*, part of his famous Khamsa, is a 12th-century Persian poem that tells the tragic tale of Qays’ all-consuming love for Layli. Their families forbid their union, leading Qays to become known as Majnun, or “the madman.” The story delves into themes of idealized love, spiritual yearning, social barriers, madness, and mystical devotion. Nizami’s elegant rendition had a lasting impact on literature and art across many cultures.", "expert_answer": "**Nizami Ganjavi’s *Layli and Majnun*** is a 12th-century Persian narrative poem, completed around **1188**, and is one of the five works in Nizami’s famous **Khamsa** (“Quintet”).\n\nIt retells the tragic Arabian love story of **Qays** and **Layli**. Qays falls deeply in love with Layli, but their families prevent their marriage. Overcome by grief and obsession, Qays becomes known as **Majnun**, meaning “madman” or “possessed.” The poem explores themes of **ideal love, spiritual longing, social constraint, madness, and mystical devotion**.\n\nNizami’s version transformed the older Arabic legend into a highly refined Persian romance and became the most influential literary treatment of the story, inspiring later poets, painters, musicians, and writers across Persian, Turkish, Urdu, and other literary traditions.", "expert_latency_s": 6.3, "stall_ms": 36, "relay_ms": 3595}
{"id": "q0484", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 2.77, "n_chunks": 3, "scores": [0.4381, 0.417, 0.4165], "eot_score": 0.2807, "eot_read_ms": 27, "reference_answer": null, "query": "电动汽车是智能交通的未来。", "transcript": "电动汽车是智能交通的未来。", "mode": "local", "answer": "Yes, electric vehicles are indeed considered a key component of the future of smart transportation. They offer several advantages that align with the goals of intelligent and sustainable urban mobility, including reduced greenhouse gas emissions, lower operating costs, improved energy efficiency, and compatibility with advanced technologies like vehicle-to-grid communication and autonomous driving systems. As part of smart traffic systems, electric vehicles can contribute to real-time data collection, traffic optimization, and integration with public transit networks—making cities cleaner, safer, and more efficient.", "answer_ms": 3053}
{"id": "q0490", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 1.8, "n_chunks": 2, "scores": [0.4268, 0.4753], "eot_score": 0.7066, "eot_read_ms": 26, "reference_answer": null, "query": "制定可追溯性计划。", "transcript": "制定可追溯性计划。", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "好的，那我给您简单说一下可追溯性计划这件事儿。简单来说，就是让项目里的每一个需求、设计、代码、测试、缺陷和变更都能互相找到对方，形成一条完整的链条。这样出了问题能快速定位，也方便审计和验证。具体怎么做呢？首先得给每个需求、任务、代码提交、测试用例这些都分配唯一的编号，比如需求叫SR-001，代码提交叫DEV-001。然后建立一个矩阵或者关系表，把需求和设计、测试用例、缺陷这些都关联起来。开发的时候，代码提交要能对应到需求或任务；测试的时候，测试用例要覆盖所有需求。过程中用一些工具，比如Jira、Git、禅道这些，把信息集中管理。最后，定期检查这些追溯关系是不是完整，有没有断链，保证每个环节都能查得到。这样一来，项目就更有条理，质量也更有保障。", "expert_answer": "以下是一份通用的**可追溯性计划**，适用于软件、系统、产品研发或项目交付过程。\n\n## 可追溯性计划\n\n### 1. 目的\n建立项目全过程的可追溯机制，确保需求、设计、开发、测试、缺陷、变更和交付成果之间能够相互关联、验证和审计。\n\n### 2. 适用范围\n本计划适用于项目生命周期内以下内容的追踪：\n\n- 用户需求\n- 系统/软件需求\n- 设计文档\n- 开发任务与代码提交\n- 测试用例与测试结果\n- 缺陷与问题单\n- 变更请求\n- 交付物与验收结果\n\n### 3. 可追溯对象\n\n| 类别 | 可追溯内容 |\n|---|---|\n| 需求 | 用户需求、业务需求、功能需求、非功能需求 |\n| 设计 | 架构设计、详细设计、接口设计 |\n| 开发 | 开发任务、代码分支、代码提交、构建版本 |\n| 测试 | 测试用例、测试执行记录、测试报告 |\n| 缺陷 | 缺陷编号、影响需求、修复记录、验证结果 |\n| 变更 | 变更申请、影响分析、审批记录、实施结果 |\n| 交付 | 版本包、发布说明、验收文档 |\n\n### 4. 可追溯关系\n\n应建立以下追溯链路：\n\n1. 用户需求 → 系统需求  \n2. 系统需求 → 设计说明  \n3. 设计说明 → 开发任务  \n4. 开发任务 → 代码提交  \n5. 系统需求 → 测试用例  \n6. 测试用例 → 测试结果  \n7. 缺陷 → 相关需求/测试用例/代码提交  \n8. 变更请求 → 受影响需求/设计/代码/测试/交付物  \n\n### 5. 编号规则\n\n建议采用统一编号方式：\n\n| 对象 | 编号示例 |\n|---|---|\n| 用户需求 | UR-001 |\n| 系统需求 | SR-001 |\n| 设计项 | DES-001 |\n| 开发任务 | DEV-001 |\n| 测试用例 | TC-001 |\n| 缺陷 | BUG-001 |\n| 变更请求 | CR-001 |\n| 交付物 | DEL-001 |\n\n### 6. 可追溯矩阵\n\n建立需求可追溯矩阵，示例如下：\n\n| 需求编号 | 需求描述 | 设计编号 | 开发任务 | 测试用例 | 缺陷编号 | 状态 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| SR-001 | 用户登录 | DES-001 | DEV-001 | TC-001 | BUG-001 | 已验证 |\n| SR-002 | 密码重置 | DES-002 | DEV-002 | TC-002 | 无 | 已通过 |\n\n### 7. 工具与存储\n\n可使用以下工具进行管理：\n\n- 需求管理：Jira、禅道、DOORS、Polarion\n- 代码管理：Git、GitLab、GitHub\n- 测试管理：TestRail、禅道、Jira\n- 文档管理：Confluence、SharePoint、SVN\n- 缺陷管理：Jira、Bugzilla、禅道\n\n所有可追溯信息应集中存储，并定期备份。\n\n### 8. 角色与职责\n\n| 角色 | 职责 |\n|---|---|\n| 项目经理 | 监督可追溯性执行情况 |\n| 需求分析师 | 维护需求及需求关系 |\n| 架构/设计人员 | 建立需求到设计的追踪关系 |\n| 开发人员 | 维护任务与代码提交关系 |\n| 测试人员 | 建立需求与测试用例、测试结果关系 |\n| 配置管理员 | 管理版本、基线和交付物 |\n| 质量人员 | 审核可追溯完整性 |\n\n### 9. 维护机制\n\n1. 新增需求时，必须分配唯一编号。\n2. 需求变更时，必须更新影响分析和追溯关系。\n3. 开发提交代码时，应关联任务或需求编号。\n4. 测试用例应覆盖对应需求。\n5. 缺陷单应关联对应测试用例、需求或代码提交。\n6. 每个阶段评审前，应检查追溯矩阵完整性。\n\n### 10. 检查与审计\n\n定期检查以下内容：\n\n- 是否所有需求都有唯一编号\n- 是否所有需求都有对应设计\n- 是否所有需求都有测试用例覆盖\n- 是否所有测试结果可追溯到需求\n- 是否所有缺陷有处理记录\n- 是否所有变更经过审批并更新追溯关系\n\n### 11. 输出物\n\n本计划执行后应形成以下成果：\n\n- 需求可追溯矩阵\n- 需求变更记录\n- 测试覆盖率报告\n- 缺陷追踪报告\n- 版本发布追溯记录\n- 可追溯性审计报告\n\n### 12. 完成标准\n\n当满足以下条件时，认为可追溯性管理有效：\n\n- 关键需求追溯覆盖率达到 100%\n- 测试用例覆盖所有已批准需求\n- 所有缺陷均可追溯到相关需求或测试用例\n- 所有变更均有审批和影响分析记录\n- 交付版本可追溯到需求、代码和测试结果", "expert_latency_s": 16.2, "stall_ms": 27, "relay_ms": 5991}
{"id": "q0495", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 3.96, "n_chunks": 4, "scores": [0.4203, 0.4072, 0.4517, 0.2853], "eot_score": 0.3546, "eot_read_ms": 30, "reference_answer": null, "query": "创建一个程序将动物分类到不同的组中。", "transcript": "创建一个程序将动物分类到不同的组中。", "mode": "local", "answer": "当然！下面是一个简单的 Python 课程示例，用于将动物分类到不同的组中。这个程序可以根据动物的特征将其分类为哺乳动物、鸟类、爬行动物、两栖动物或鱼类。我们使用一个简单的基于名称的分类方法，后续可以扩展为更复杂的分类系统，比如根据生物学特征或用户输入的更多细节进行分类，但这里先从基础开始，适合初学者学习和理解分类逻辑的基础概念，比如条件判断、字典和函数等编程知识，这些都是计算机科学中数据分类和组织的重要基础，有助于培养算法思维和问题解决能力，是计算机科学教育中的重要组成部分，能够帮助学生理解如何对复杂信息进行结构化处理，为后续学习更高级的机器学习或数据库设计打下基础，同时也能激发他们对生物分类学的兴趣，促进跨学科的学习。", "answer_ms": 5559}
{"id": "q0506", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 2.33, "n_chunks": 3, "scores": [0.455, 0.4054, 0.4567], "eot_score": 0.2175, "eot_read_ms": 27, "reference_answer": null, "query": "为什么自我关怀很重要？", "transcript": "为什么自我关怀很重要？", "mode": "local", "answer": "自我关怀非常重要，因为它有助于我们建立更健康、更积极的自我关系，从而提升整体的心理和生理健康。以下是几个关键原因，解释为什么自我关怀如此重要：1. 提升心理健康：当我们学会关心自己，而不是苛责自己，就能减少焦虑、抑郁和压力。自我关怀能帮助我们以更温和、理解的态度面对挫折和困难，增强心理韧性。2. 促进情绪调节：自我关怀能帮助我们更好地识别和接纳自己的情绪，而不是压抑或否认它们。当我们感到疲惫、悲伤或愤怒时，给予自己支持和安慰，有助于更快恢复情绪平衡。3. 提高生活质量：关心自己的身体和情感需求——比如好好吃饭、休息、运动、表达感受——能让我们更有能量去应对生活中的挑战，也更容易建立健康的人际关系。4. 对抗完美主义：许多人在成长过程中学会了过度自我批评。自我关怀鼓励我们接纳不完美，允许自己犯错，从而减少因追求完美而带来的巨大压力。5. 以身作则：当我们学会自我关怀，也会更自然地将这种态度带到与他人的互动中，培养同理心和关爱他人。总结来说，自我关怀不是自私，而是一种必要的自我照顾方式。它让我们像对待真正关心我们的人那样，善待自己。正如心理学家Kristin Neff所说：“我们对自己有爱，才能真正爱别人。”", "answer_ms": 9053}
